<title>USA: Brazil to stay course on monetary policy - Loyola.</title>
<headline>Brazil to stay course on monetary policy - Loyola.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's central bank president Gustavo Loyola said on Friday the bank has no plans to change monetary policy or speed up the gradual depreciation of the real currency because of the country's international trade deficit.</p>
<p>Loyola told Reuters before a conference here that Brazil's trade situation was &quot;very good&quot; and there was no need to change exchange rate policy or slow the pace of interest rate cuts.</p>
<p>-- N.A. Treasury Desk 212-859-1871</p>
</text>
